{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792489339,"nonce":"AO6zUD7I6K7i1gCWdpsgSQm7YiM=","message":"**RayDE after every tab is closed (user report: 550 MB)**\n\nMeasured with the scratch driver that opens 30 of RayDE's own source files in its Workbench one after another, then calls closeAll(), with footprint -p and vmmap -summary:\n- an empty window, settled: 327 MB (3,908 styled elements, of which 429 command-palette items with their labels and icons are built while the palette is closed)\n- 30 tabs open: 470 to 520 MB at rest\n- all closed and a major collection: 424 to 451 MB\n\nClosing does hand the tabs back: styled elements return to 3,908, canvases to 0, and RayDE's document, buffer and editorRef maps to 0. The 100 MB above the empty window is not live tab state. malloc_zone_pressure_relief reclaims nothing, so the pages hold live data. Allocation call trees (malloc_history on a debug library) attribute the growth to the Ash JIT (cranelift and LLVM structures, LLVM debug-info metadata, roughly 25 MB), Haxe int hash tables, Ash heap blocks and about 6 MB of blinc_abi allocator blocks.\n\n**What the floor is made of**\n\nThe empty window's 327 MB is MALLOC_SMALL about 140 MB, the Ash heap about 115 MB, IOSurface 32 MB and MALLOC_LARGE about 17 MB, for 3,908 elements: roughly 80 KB each. Building the command palette's rows only while it is open would remove about a third of the elements. That is RayDE's code.\n\n**Found on the way**\n\nAn inline flow kept its pieces' owners after dropping them, leaving 135 breadcrumb Texts in Text.byNode (f52a0e2). Fixed; it is a few MB at most.","files":null}]}